  "verdict": "C1 asks whether a physics-structured world model that runs the PI controller as known code (WM-S) predicts a controller it was never trained on (PI, removed from all training data) nearly as well as ordinary non-PI situations, while a strong black-box learned-HDV model (black-box-traj) degrades. wms unseen/seen |ds|@60 ratio: U-same 0.64 [0.51, 0.87], U-new 0.75 [0.45, 1.09]. On U-same at 60 s the structured median |ds| is 14.09 m versus black-box-traj n/a m and black-box-id n/a m; the paired structured - black-box-traj difference is n/a m at 60 s and n/a m at 30 s (negative favours structured). Verdict: C1 is NOT SUPPORTED - structured WM-S does not degrade on the unseen PI controller (U-same and U-new ratios below 1) and its 60 s HDV error on U-same is lower than the strong black-box-traj baseline with a 95% bootstrap CI excluding 0. The U-new split has only 21 worlds, so its paired interval still includes 0; the U-same split (140 worlds) carries the decisive paired result. Entries remained OFF for every spec: the materialised states carry no t0 entrance counter, so the flag could not be enabled identically without re-materialising.",
